You learn something new every day...

Is this effect new to 3.1.x?  I don't recall seeing it in the 
spoilers for 3.0j.  

Ah...there it is in the new (partial) 3.1 spoiler (I really should read
that thing).  I've never seen this posted before.  Since I noticed this 
in the spoilers, I consider this the best spoiler I've seen posted in a
while.  (Sorry if everyone else already knew this).  When Boudewijn first 
asked the question, I was about to write back, "There's no such thing as 
a magic fountain -- the effects from drinking for a fountain are just 
random."

According to the source one in 7 fountains is blessed/magic.  If your 
luck is 4 or more, a blessed fountain has a 2/3 chance of both restoring 
your ability and increasing all your abilities - following this, the
fountain becomes a normal fountain.  The remaining 1/3 of the time, you
get a message "the cool draught refreshes you", and the fountain stays 
blessed.

Other things:
------------
- No way to tell that a fountain is blessed without quaffing (you'd
  think a Priest would be able to tell).
- You can wish for a magic fountain in wizard mode.
- Any fountain always has a 1/7 chance of being blessed (even the ones
  on special levels - I thought maybe some might always be blessed, but 
  no such luck.  It'd be kind of neat if one in the oracle room [or 
  somewhere] were always blessed).
- No special effects for dipping things in a blessed fountain.

Hmmm... I wonder if cursed fountains are coming in 3.1.4.  Could be 
interesting if you knew that one of the fountains in the mine town
was blessed and one was cursed, but had no way of knowing, and the
guards wouldn't want you to use them in any case.  It'd be an 
interesting problem for a nethacker to try to solve.  If there were
both cursed and blessed maybe there'd be some way of noticing that
a fountain were one or the other, but no way to tell which.  Maybe
using warning (an otherwise useless intrinsic) and a luckstone.

-------------------- possible 3.1.4 scenario:
You see here a fountain.  You luckstone quivers.
You quaff a potion of make invisible.
You quaff at the fountain (the gaurds don't see you)
ACCK! This water's no good!  You feel weak!  You feel stupid! -- more --
You feel foolish! You feel clumsy! You feel vulnerable! -- more --
You feel Ugly!  The water's flow is reduced. -- more --
A guard notices the reduced flow, and stands on top of the second fountain. 
